=============================
TIME & SPACE COMPLEXITY NOTES
=============================

---------------------------------
1) BASIC LOOPS
---------------------------------

for loop
TC = O(n)
SC = O(1)

Example:
for(int i=0;i<n;i++)

-----------------------------

nested loop

for(i=0 to n)
   for(j=0 to n)

TC = O(n²)
SC = O(1)

-----------------------------

triple nested loop

TC = O(n³)

-----------------------------

loop running half times

for(i=0;i<n/2;i++)

TC = O(n)

(ignore constants)

-----------------------------

logarithmic loop

for(i=1;i<n;i*=2)

TC = O(log n)

Example:
1 → 2 → 4 → 8 → 16

-----------------------------

divide by 2 loop

while(n>0)
   n=n/2

TC = O(log n)

---------------------------------
2) ARRAYS
---------------------------------

Access by index
arr[i]

TC = O(1)

-----------------------------

Linear search

TC = O(n)

-----------------------------

Binary Search (sorted array)

TC = O(log n)
SC = O(1)

Recursive binary search:
SC = O(log n)

-----------------------------

Traversing array

TC = O(n)

---------------------------------
3) SORTING
---------------------------------

Bubble Sort

Best = O(n)
Average = O(n²)
Worst = O(n²)

SC = O(1)

-----------------------------

Selection Sort

Best/Average/Worst = O(n²)

SC = O(1)

-----------------------------

Insertion Sort

Best = O(n)
Worst = O(n²)

SC = O(1)

-----------------------------

Merge Sort

TC = O(n log n)
SC = O(n)

-----------------------------

Quick Sort

Best = O(n log n)
Average = O(n log n)
Worst = O(n²)

SC = O(log n)

---------------------------------
4) RECURSION
---------------------------------

Simple recursion

func(n-1)

TC = O(n)
SC = O(n)

Example:
print(5)

-----------------------------

Binary recursion

func(n-1)
func(n-1)

TC = O(2^n)

SC = O(n)

Example:
subset recursion

-----------------------------

Fibonacci recursion

fib(n-1)+fib(n-2)

TC = O(2^n)
SC = O(n)

-----------------------------

Recursion tree formula

TC =
(total nodes) ×
(work at each node)

---------------------------------
5) BACKTRACKING
---------------------------------

Subset / Subsequence

TC = O(2^n * n)
SC = O(n)

Reason:
2^n subsets
printing = n

-----------------------------

Permutation

TC = O(n! * n)
SC = O(n)

Reason:
n! permutations
print takes O(n)

---------------------------------
6) HASHING
---------------------------------

HashMap

Insert = O(1)
Search = O(1)
Delete = O(1)

Worst = O(n)

-----------------------------

HashSet

Average = O(1)

---------------------------------
7) STACK / QUEUE
---------------------------------

Push = O(1)
Pop = O(1)
Peek = O(1)

---------------------------------
8) LINKED LIST
---------------------------------

Insert at head = O(1)

Delete at head = O(1)

Search = O(n)

Access nth element = O(n)

---------------------------------
9) TREES
---------------------------------

DFS

TC = O(n)
SC = O(h)

h = height

-----------------------------

BFS

TC = O(n)
SC = O(n)

-----------------------------

Balanced BST

Search = O(log n)

Worst skew tree:

O(n)

---------------------------------
10) GRAPHS
---------------------------------

DFS

TC = O(V + E)

SC = O(V)

-----------------------------

BFS

TC = O(V + E)

SC = O(V)

---------------------------------
11) BIG O IMPORTANT RULES
---------------------------------

O(1)  -> constant
O(log n) -> best scalable
O(n) -> linear
O(n log n) -> very good
O(n²) -> heavy
O(2^n) -> very expensive
O(n!) -> worst

---------------------------------
12) IGNORE IN BIG O
---------------------------------

Constants ignored

O(2n) = O(n)

O(100n) = O(n)

-----------------------------

Lower terms ignored

O(n²+n)

= O(n²)

O(n³+n²+n)

= O(n³)

---------------------------------
13) QUICK RECOGNITION TRICKS
---------------------------------

One loop
→ O(n)

Nested loop
→ O(n²)

Divide by 2
→ O(log n)

Recursion with 2 calls
→ O(2^n)

Permutation
→ O(n!)

Merge sort style
→ O(n log n)